:: Livestock Dewintering 2
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is 0>>
	Remy whistles, and some of the herd moo in response. A <<livestock_horse>> clops up to the open barn doors. Remy boards the <<livestock_horse>> and scans the barn.
	<br><br>
	<<if $livestock.obey gte 80>>
		"Move <<phim>> up front," <<he>> calls. A farmhand nudges you forward through the herd until you stand at the front. You glance at the other <<livestock_cows>>. They almost seem to salivate at the fresh, green grass. <<if $cow gte 6>>The thought of it makes you salivate too<<else>>Your mouth almost dries up at the prospect of eating grass, but it's arguably more appetising than hay<</if>>.
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $livestock.obey gte 60>>
		"<<pShes>> been good. Move <<phim>> up," <<he>> calls. A farmhand nudges you, and you stumble forward, displacing a few other <<livestock_cows>>. They moo in discontent, but they are quickly quieted by the other farmhands. From where you stand, you can see the green grass of the field. No doubt the rest of the herd is excited. <<if $cow gte 6>>It looks lush and delicious<<else>>It isn't appetising, but anything would be better than dry hay<</if>>.
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $livestock.obey gte 40>>
		"Push <<phim>> in a bit," <<he>> calls. A farmhand nudges you inward, and you now are surrounded by other members of the herd. You can't tell what lies ahead, but the fresh air would be nice.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	Remy nods, then blows a whistle around <<his>> neck. You don't hear anything, but the dogs begin to bark, and the cows are quick to respond. The ground is wet beneath your feet, and the fields are expansive past the gates. Somehow, it looks bigger than before.
	<br><br>
	Remy pauses, riding in front of the herd. Some farmhands follow with baskets of apples, giving one apple to each cow.
	<br><br>
	<<if $livestock.obey gte 30>>
		Remy stops in front of you. <span class="green">"Give <<phim>> one too.<<if C.npc.Remy.love gte 80>> The <<girl>> deserves it for all <<pshe>> makes.<</if>>"</span>
		<br>
		Following orders, a farmhand gives you an apple. The juice is sweet, and it leaves you craving more.<<stress -10>><<lstress>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	Remy rides back to the side and dismounts. <<He>> slides a key into the lock on the gate, then pushes it open. <<livestock_cows>> moo with delight as they run past you. They almost seem to be frolicking. You hesitate at the gate, letting the rest of the herd go first.
	<br><br>
	"Go on, <<girl>>. The grass tastes better than hay," Remy says. When you don't respond, <<he>> slaps your <<bottomsimple>>, and you lurch forward enough for <<him>> to close the gate. With a heavy click, the gates lock you inside.
<<else>>
	Remy turns away from you and whistles. <<His>> <<livestock_horse>> approaches as the dogs begin to bark, startling the cattle. Moos fill the barn as they jostle past you.
	<br><br>
	The <<person2>><<person>> and <<person3>><<person>> hold you in place as Remy approaches you. "I have half a mind to keep you in this barn until you behave," <<person1>><<he>> says. "I can't spare the resources, however. So you'll be at the back of the herd instead." <<He>> mounts <<his>> <<livestock_horse>> without another word.
	<br><br>
	The <<person4>><<person>> nudges you until you go to the back of the herd. You follow them through the farm, looking around as you do. The farmhands are relaxing with beers and pastries. Some ignore the herd. Others pay a little too much attention.
	<br><br>
	Remy dismounts and opens the gate to the field. The herd charges through, mooing with delight. A few even kick their legs as they start searching for the tastiest tufts of grass. <<if $cow gte 6>>After a winter of dry hay, your mouth waters<<else>>You look at them with contempt<</if>>.
	<br><br>
	Soon you're the only one still outside the field. Remy's green eyes glimmer as <<person1>><<he>> regards you. "If you were a good <<girl>>, this wouldn't be necessary," <<he>> says. "Best remember your place."
	<br><br>
